      <div itemprop="text">
        <p>Yes, but you need OCR (Optical Character Recognition) as an intermediate step. The cheapest free method: upload the scanned PDF to Google Docs, which runs OCR automatically, then export as EPUB using File → Download → EPUB. For batch processing, use Tesseract OCR with Pandoc on the command line. Note that OCR accuracy varies — clean scans of standard fonts can achieve 99%+ accuracy, while handwritten text or unusual fonts may need manual correction.</p>
      </div>
