  <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
    <h3 itemprop="name">What is the best free software for batch PDF to EPUB conversion?</h3>
    <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
      <div itemprop="text">
        <p>Calibre is the best free tool for batch conversion. Add multiple PDFs to your library, select them all, and click "Convert books → Bulk convert." Calibre processes them sequentially and preserves metadata across the batch. For command-line batch processing, use Pandoc with a simple shell script: <code>for f in *.pdf; do pandoc "$f" -o "\${f%.pdf}.epub"; done</code>. This converts every PDF in the current directory to EPUB.</p>
      </div>
